{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_cgrid_bound_coriolis_v",
    "description": "The bound_coriolis north-face Coriolis + momentum-advection acceleration of the mom6_cgrid: CAv(i,j,k) = clamp(pvf_v(i,j,k), min(fu1..fu4), max(fu1..fu4)) - KEy(i,j,k), the MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc bound_Coriolis law (the fu1..fu4 bounds and the min/max clamp at :1139-1150, then the -d(KE)/dy term of the KEy loop): fu1 = -av(i,j,k)*u(i,j+1,k), fu2 = -av(i,j,k)*u(i,j,k), fu3 = -av(i-1,j,k)*u(i-1,j+1,k), fu4 = -av(i-1,j,k)*u(i-1,j,k), the -av*u products at the four q-points around the north face (av the absolute vorticity at the q-points, u the east-face velocities of the two cells on each side of the face), with the raw potential-vorticity flux pvf_v (the sibling mom6_cgrid_pvf_v rule) clamped to the local bound and the meridional KE gradient KEy subtracted (clamp(x, lo, hi) = min(max(x, lo), hi) is exact — max/min select without rounding, so the Fortran's min-then-max sequence produces identical bits). SOLID-WALL BOUNDARIES: the west domain edge (i = 1) and the north domain edge (j = N_J) carry a zero-gradient halo, so the wall regions MIRROR the out-of-bounds neighbor onto the edge cell itself: the i = 1 region reads av(1,j,k)/u(1,j,k) in place of av(0,j,k)/u(0,j,k) and the j = N_J region reads u(i,N_J,k) in place of u(i,N_J+1,k) (the NW corner mirrors both) — NOT clamped reads of nonexistent cells. The rule is a named-op rule (esm-spec 9.6.8), applied once per consumer equation as mom6_cgrid_bound_coriolis_v(pvf_v, av, u, KEy); all four params must be declared [i,j,k] fields (esm-spec 9.6.1 where clause).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:mom6_cgrid",
      "grid:mom6_cgrid",
      "op:clamp",
      "order:0",
      "bc:wall",
      "axes:i,j,k"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
      },
      {
        "citation": "MOM6 source: MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc bound_Coriolis fu1..fu4 :1139-1150 and the -d(KE)/dy term; the face conventions of the mom6_cgrid grid.esm."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
